  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${\u222c}_{R}\\frac{1}{xy}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[1,e]\\times [e,{e}^{2}].$",
  "worked_solution": "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{R}\\frac{1}{xy}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\u222c}_{R}(\\frac{1}{x})\\text{\u00a0}(\\frac{1}{y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x]_{1}^{e}\\cdot [\\operatorname{ln}\u2061y]_{e}^{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061e-\\operatorname{ln}\u20611)\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{e}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061e) \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
